# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values.
# See README.md → "Environment variables" for where each value comes from.
# The defaults run the Website and the Admin on in-memory sample data, with no
# backend. Fill in the Supabase and database lines to run `pnpm dev` against
# the hosted project, with Google sign-in (README → Admin → Signing in locally).
# No test reads them: e2e blanks them, and CI uses a local Supabase.

# ── App ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public base URL of the site. In production set this to your real domain.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Optional: shown in metadata. Usually your app version or a git sha.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_VERSION=

# ── Logging ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One of: NONE | ERROR | WARN | DEBUG | ALL
NEXT_PUBLIC_LOG_LEVEL=ALL

# ── Auth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only SUPABASE is wired in this template.
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_STRATEGY=SUPABASE

# ── Supabase ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# For development, the hosted project (Project Settings → API Keys); or, with a
# local Supabase (`pnpm db:start`), what `supabase status` prints. With these
# and DATABASE_URL all set, the Admin runs live and Staff sign in with Google.
# Never commit the values: .env is git-ignored.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<ref>.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_…
# SERVER-ONLY secret (src/env.server.ts), used for Storage only: the photo
# uploads, their clean-up, and `pnpm catalogue:seed` (so `pnpm db:reset` too).
# With DATABASE_URL set and this unset, photo uploads fail. It bypasses RLS:
# never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC and never reference it from client code.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_…

# Local Supabase only: the Google provider in supabase/config.toml reads these
# (the app never does). It's off unless ENABLED is "true", with a client id
# and secret from a Google OAuth client; then `pnpm db:start` again. The hosted
# project keeps its own in the Supabase dashboard (the runbook, step 8).
SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_ENABLED=
SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Database (Drizzle) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SERVER-ONLY secret — never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC and never reference it from
# client code (it is validated apart in src/env.server.ts).
# For development on the hosted project, its SESSION POOLER string (Dashboard →
# Connect → Session pooler, IPv4), port 5432:
#   postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@<pooler-host>:5432/postgres
# Not the direct connection (db.<ref>.supabase.co): it's IPv6-only, and many
# home networks can't reach it. With a local Supabase, the database
# `pnpm db:start` runs (postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres).
# In production (Vercel only), the hosted TRANSACTION POOLER string (port 6543):
#   postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@<pooler-host>:6543/postgres
# `pnpm db:check` checks the database it names, read-only.
# Leave this UNSET to run on the in-memory mock (the default) — the app builds
# and runs with no database configured.
# DATABASE_URL=

# ── Database tests ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `pnpm test:db` (and `pnpm test`) run the database tests against this, never
# against DATABASE_URL. Unset or unreachable ⇒ they are skipped with the reason.
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres
# Local Supabase's Secret key, for the Storage tests (the bucket, uploads, the
# seed's photos, the clean-up). Unset ⇒ they are skipped with the reason.
# TEST_SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=your-local-secret-key

# ── End-to-end tests ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset (the default), `pnpm test:e2e` runs on the in-memory sample data. CI
# sets all four from the runner's local Supabase to run the Admin live; any
# host but this machine is refused. Never the hosted project.
# PLAYWRIGHT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres
# PLAYWRIGHT_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
# PLAYWRIGHT_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-local-publishable-key
# PLAYWRIGHT_SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=your-local-secret-key

# ── Member App switch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SERVER-ONLY. Leave it unset in production until launch.
# Off by default: unset or "false" hides every Member App button,
# link and message on the Website ("Sign in", "Start reviewing", the app
# announcement, …). Set to "true" when the Member App launches. Any other value
# fails the boot. Flipping it needs a redeploy or restart, not a code change.
MEMBER_APP_LIVE=false

# ── PostHog analytics (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The whole integration is INERT unless NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY is set (no init,
# no network). The project token is PUBLISHABLE (not a secret), so NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# is correct — do NOT put it in a server-only file. Client ingestion is proxied
# same-origin via the `/relay` reverse proxy (next.config.ts rewrites) to keep
# the strict CSP unchanged and dodge ad-blockers.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_your_project_token
# Real ingestion host for the SERVER SDK (US default; EU variant shown):
#   US: https://us.i.posthog.com   ·   EU: https://eu.i.posthog.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
# The Website runs cookieless and anonymous with no consent banner (ADR 0009):
# nothing is stored on the device and capture starts on load. In the PostHog
# project settings, also turn on "Discard client IP data".
